  "articleBody": "A kitchen door that sticks occasionally might seem like a simple nuisance, but frame issues often point to deeper concerns that hinge adjustments cannot resolve. Knowing when to step back and call a qualified professional prevents costly damage to your kitchen walls and flooring.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- Soft, crumbling jamb bases: Kitchen floors experience frequent washing, spills, and plumbing humidity. If pressing a finger or screwdriver into the lower door frame feels spongy, moisture rot has set in and the wood can no longer support hinge screws.\n- Major diagonal racking: When you measure diagonally from opposite corners and find significant differences, the rough opening has shifted. Forcing the door to close under these conditions will eventually warp the door slab.\n- Cracking drywall around the casing: Hairline or widening cracks extending from the top corners of your door frame into the kitchen wall often indicate structural movement or shifted framing studs.\n- Loose hinge screws that spin freely: Stripped screw holes in settled framing require deeper anchoring or structural blocking, not just larger screws.\n\nReplacing the door slab before diagnosing a misaligned frame wastes time and money. Abraham Becerra and the crew at HH Remodeling LLC handle door frame repairs, framing, and drywall restoration throughout the Denver area. Call 303-505-0866 to resolve your door frame issues.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
